From: CHEN Xuan <chenxuan@iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] Mark the target-kind registry node as non-copyable

System TVM FFI 0.1.10 automatically registers shallow-copy methods for
copy-constructible reflected nodes. The unordered_map copy trait does not
inspect its unique_ptr-containing values, so TargetKindNode incorrectly
appears copyable until the copy body is instantiated. Declare its existing
non-copyable semantics explicitly and retain default construction.

Upstream FFI behavior: https://github.com/apache/tvm-ffi/pull/438
The newer TVM target-config refactor is not a minimal backport:
https://github.com/apache/tvm/pull/18788
No matching upstream fix found; this adapts the bundled TVM to system FFI.

--- a/3rdparty/tvm/include/tvm/target/target_kind.h
+++ b/3rdparty/tvm/include/tvm/target/target_kind.h
@@ -66,6 +66,11 @@
 /*! \brief Target kind, specifies the kind of the target */
 class TargetKindNode : public Object {
  public:
+  TargetKindNode() = default;
+  // The registry owns unique type metadata; this node cannot be copied.
+  TargetKindNode(const TargetKindNode&) = delete;
+  TargetKindNode& operator=(const TargetKindNode&) = delete;
+
   /*! \brief Name of the target kind */
   ffi::String name;
   /*! \brief Device type of target kind */
